<tei:div corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:prayer:birkat_hachodesh/yehi_ratzon"><tei:pb n="382" ed="1949 shabbat/shacharit/torah" facs="https://archive.org/download/PhilipBirnbaumHaSiddurHaShalemTheDailyPrayerBook1949/page/n406_medium.jpg"/><tei:p><tei:milestone unit="prayer-part" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:prayer:birkat_hachodesh/yehi_ratzon/text"/>May it be thy will, Lord our God and God of our fathers, to grant us this new month for happiness and blessedness. O grant us long life, a life of peace and well-being, a life of blessing and sustenance, a life of physical health, a life of piety and dread of sin, a life free from shame and disgrace, a life of wealth and honor, a life marked by our love for Torah and our fear of Heaven, a life in which the wishes of our heart shall be fulfilled for happiness. Amen. <tei:milestone unit="prayer-part"/></tei:p></tei:div>
